{
	"_comment": "Synthetic scenes for the anti-sleep auto-clicker matcher (_shared/shortcuts/engine/auto_click_matcher.lua and its Windows twin). A template is rows of characters mapped through palette to gray values. A scene is a width x height image filled with background, plus noise drawn from the Park-Miller generator (state = state * 16807 mod 2147483647, starting at seed; each pixel in row-major order adds state mod (2 * amplitude + 1) - amplitude, then clamps to 0..255), then each paste writes the template at its top-left x, y, enlarged or reduced by its power-of-two scale, with delta added to every pixel and clamped. overlay_noise, when present, is drawn the same way after the pastes, so a pasted button no longer matches exactly. A vector's template may itself be scaled (template_scale) to stand for a capture made at another density. expect is the match (top-left x, y, width, height in scene pixels and the scale factor tried on the template) or null; reason is the refusal reason when there is one. A vector with score_near also pins the best score to within 1e-6, and its threshold sits just under or over it.",
